e  This fibrous tissue approaches the posterior  lateral  and superior margins  The specimen is approximately 80  fibrous and 20  fatty  No biopsy cavity or tumor are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Posterior margin  C  Superior margin  D  Inferior margin  E  Anterior margin  F  Lateral margin  G  Medial margin  H K  Representative of fibrous tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fibro fatty breast tissue  which is entirely submitted in cassettes L R  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of adipose tissue within which are multiple tan yellow lymph nodes ranging from 0 2cm to 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  S DD  Whole lymph nodes EE GG  Representative sectins of lymph nodes  Gross Description by  SHANNON SCHUTZ Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT BREAST LUMP   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS    EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 22 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SCATTERED SMALL FOCI  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  RADIAL SCARS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma grows as scattered small nodules  It is therefore impossible to determine the size of the invasive carcinoma  The infiltrating carcinoma probbably aggregates to less than 1cm  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  BREAST  RIGHT   INFERIOR MARGIN    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor appears different from the tumor in the mastectomy specimen  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 12 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   SEPARATELY SUBMITTED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  RIGHT   INFERIOR MARGIN    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast biopsy  are multiple white to yellow core biopsies  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm in aggregate  entirely frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm piece of tan  rubbery soft tissue  frozen entirely as frozen section  2  resubmitted in cassette B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  with R