dictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 58    REVISED REMOVED_DATE        RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast lesion  are two fragments of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The larger specimen  with two wires  is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm well circumscribed tan mass  0 2cm from the margin and the second mass 0 5cm at the margin  The second  smaller  specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  Section code  A B  first mass C  second mass D F  additional sections from first fragment G J  second fragment  entirely submitted Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST   MASS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST   CALCIFICATIONS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
