ors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast mass  is a 5 x 4 x 2 8cm portion of breast parenchyma with two black sutures  The long suture designates the lateral aspect of the specimen while the short suture the superior  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan to brown scirrhous lesion with stellate radicals which extend out into the surrounding tissue  The tumor extends to within 0 7cm of the closest deep margin  which is 3 5cm medial to the lateral margin of the specimen  Within this specimen there are scattered foci of dense fibrosis  A representative section of such an area is taken  Tissue is taken for frozen section and saved frozen  Section Code A   closest deep margin B   additional deep margin C   closest superior margin D E   additional tumor F   representative section of fibrosis G   representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left axilla contents  is a 10 x 6 x 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 0 4cm aggregate of tan to red lymph nodes are dissected from the specimen and submitted with one of the nodes being suspicious for metastatic disease found in I  The remainder of the lymph nodes are found in H K  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GROSSLY APPROACHING TO APPROXIMATELY 0 7CM FROM THE CLOSEST MA