Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 92 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 16 12 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MASS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  65   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  35    NOTE  Carcinoma abuts upon the margin  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The intraductal carcinoma is mostly comedo or solid type  it extends beyond areas of invasive carcinoma  The carcinoma has some features suggestive of lobular carcinoma  many signet ring cells  some small cells in the infiltrating component   but overall the features are most consistent with ductal carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 16 19                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 14 26     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining of 100 breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory we also compared the results of staining of 50 breast carcinomas for progesterone receptor protein with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   is a 6 x 3 x 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  Sectioning reveals an ill defined  firm  white  focally gritty area  2 5cm in diameter  extending to the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue for estrogen receptor studies is taken  Representative sections submitted in A through J  Resident  Jane M  Yang  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Edwin Post Maynard  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
