Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  INVOLVING A MARGIN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20    LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE TUMOR  PRESENT AT MARGINS  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  SEVERAL FOCI  PRESENT AT MARGINS  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN   BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  SEVERAL FOCI  PRESENT AT MARGINS  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL MARGIN   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  AND FOCAL LUTEAL CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  TWO SEPARATE NODULES  EACH REMOVED_DATE CM  ALONG THE SAME TISSUE MARGIN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SOLID AND MICROPAPILLARY TYPES  PRESENT AT A MARGIN  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN   BIOPSY  ADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of tissue with a rubbery 0 4cm nodule  The adjacent areas are somewhat irregular  Entirely submitted in cassettes A and B  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are five more separate specimens  Labelled  A   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked  all submitted in cassette C  Labelled  B   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked and all submitted in cassette D  Labelled  C   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked and entirely submitted in cassette E  Labelled  D   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue inked and entirely submitted in cassette F  Labelled  E   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm piece of fibroadipose 