Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 14 08 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 23 OF 23 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13 51                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm aggregate of adipose within which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 2cm to 4 0cm in greatest dimension  Sections are submitted as follows  A F  Whole lymph nodes G  Representative of a lymph node H  Representative of a lymph node I J  Representative of 4 0cm node Received fresh  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast excision   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan pink skin ellipse  The skin has a 3 5cm well healed incision site  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  deep  black  superior  blue  lateral  orange  medial  red  and inferior green  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm area which is centrally cystic and surrounded by fat necrosis and fibrosis  This area is directly subjacent to the incision and is consistent with a biopsy cavity  This biopsy cavity abuts the superior mar