Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 12 28 CLINICAL DATA  History of ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  INVOLVING AN INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Scattered small foci  involving 4 of 10 blocks and spanning at least 1 3cm Grade  1 Calcifications  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to 0 15cm from the black inked margin of the specimen in one focus  Diagnosis by  SELIM NASSER  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 19 53                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with two localization wires in place and a corresponding radiograph  The specimen is inked black and is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan red well circumscribed healing biopsy site which comes to 0 1cm of the margin  Adjacent to the nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm indurated grey white gritty lesion which comes to 0 5cm of the margin  The remaining cut surface consist of 15  dense grey white fibrous tissue and 85  tan yellow adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  healing biopsy site C F  gritty mass with area designated localization wires as C D  G J  additional fibroadipose tissue Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  VINCENT KO  MD                                                                    