ed the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch marking the lateral tail  The anterior is inked blue  and the posterior is inked black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm tan skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nipple areola complex which is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominantly fibrous breast parenchyma with diffuse fibrocystic changes  No discrete masses or previous biopsy sites are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative upper inner quadrant to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral  axillary  tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections from upper inner quadrant  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  1  620   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm lymph node with attached adipose tissue  The node is bisected  and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node  2  425   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node with attached adipose tissue  The node is bisected  and entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  The specimen was re examined and additional tissue sections were submitted for histologic examination  These sections reveal an additional small focus of grade 1 ductal carcinoma in situ  spanning 0 1cm   on which hormone receptor studies will be performed  Other findings include atypic