Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 AUG 03 ACCESSIONED ON  12 AUG 03 at 15 46 CLINICAL DATA  Left axillary sentinel lymph node biopsy for staging  Poorly differentiated carcinoma with signet ring cells with focal lymphatic invasion  Left simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODES  LEFT SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Numerous scattered tumor cells  hundreds per lymph node  are identified in the subcapsular sinuses of both lymph nodes  on H E and confirmatory cytokeratin immunostains  Extranodal involvement is not seen  When evaluated in conjunction with the permanent sections  scattered tumor cells can be identified on the frozen section slides  However  in isolation  the frozen section findings are not felt to be definitive  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  PLEOMORPHIC TYPE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The signet ring cell morphology seen in the core biopsy is not as prominent now that the complete tumor is available for evaluation  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm Grade  3 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present Blood vessel invasion  Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater Stains for receptors  Requested Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  15 AUG 03 at 15 52                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block G   Few tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 AUG 03 at 13 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel lymph node  are two fibrofatty tissues measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  entirely frozen as FX 1 and FX 2  submitted now in cassettes A B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 25 x 14 x 4 5cm simple mastectomy with a 25 x 10 6cm skin ellipse and nipple  There is a suture at one edge of the skin ellipse demarcating 12 o clock  A large mass can be palpated beneath the skin superior and lateral to the nipple  The anterior surgical margin is inked blue and the posterior surgical margin is inked black  Sectioning through the breast reveals a tan pink cerebriform mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  which is 3cm from the posterior margin  3cm from the 6 o clock anterior margin  2cm from the 12 o clock anterior margin and 1 0cm from the skin  No nodes were palpated in the specimen  Representative sections are submitted as follows  C  Closest anterior margin along the 6 o clock edge of the specimen  D  Closest anterior margin along the 12 o clock edge of the specimen  E  Closest posterior margin  F  Closest skin margin  G J  Breast mass  K L  Uninvolved breast tissue  Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  LYMPH NODES  LEFT SENTINEL   REACTIVE FOLLICULAR HYPERPLASIA