has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right sentinel node   is a piece of oval shaped  pink tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Portions of fat are dissected to reveal 3 distinct nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0 7cm in largest dimension and having a rubbery consistency  The lymph nodes are entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents   is a 22 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right mastectomy specimen with attached 8 x 6 x 1 7cm axillary tissue  which is marked by a stitch  There is an attached REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nipple  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior is inked black  After removal of the axillary tail  the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm stellate  tan pink lesion in a lower inner quadrant of the specimen  2 0cm from the medial edge of the specimen and 0 5cm from the posterior resection margin and 0 8cm from the nearest anterior resection margin  This stellate area is continuous with REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm circumscribed  hard  tan solid area that comes 0 3cm to the nearest posterior margin and is 1 5cm from the nearest anterior resection margin  Superior to that area  there is separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hard stellate tan lesion that is partially bridging to the solid area and is separated from it by 2 5cm  The second stellate lesion is greater than 1 5cm from the nearest resection margin  posterior   The rest of the breast tissue is tan  lobular with fat containing focal areas of hemorrhage in the lateral aspect there is a 0 5cm ill defined cavity with smooth surface and slight green discoloration  It is 1 8cm from the nearest posterior resection margin  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the medial most stellate lesion including the anterior and the posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the solid area lateral to the first stellate lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the second stellate lesion including a section towards the nearest posterior resection margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of the ill defined cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative section of the breast away from the lesions  The axillary tail is dissected from lymph nodes and potential lymph nodes are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two potential lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One potential lymph nodes  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  RIGHT   METASTATIC CARCINOMA  SEVERAL SMALL FOCI   1 MM   IN ONE NODE AND A SUBCAPSULAR FOCUS APPROXIMATELY 3 MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION IN A SECOND NODE  MORE TUMOR IS SEEN ON THE DEEPER SECTIONS THAN ON FIRST SECTION   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  CRYOSTAT FROZEN SECTION  SLIDE ONLY  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 31 CLINICAL DATA  48 year old female with infiltrating ductal carcinoma of left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   1   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  1    LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE FOCUS  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  SEE NOTE  2   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  1  In areas the tumor has a tubular pattern  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma is within 0 1cm of the inked superior resection margin  The tumor is 0 9cm in greatest dimension no lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is identified  The single focus of LCIS  slide M  is 0 3cm from a superior margin  NOTE  2  The focus of lobular carcinoma in situ is within 0 1cm of the closest inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 20 01 Consulting Pathologist s   Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  in three separately labeled parts  Labeled  left  breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of yellow tan fibroadipose tissue with 2 attached sutures  a long one designating the lateral aspect and a short one designating the superior aspect  The superior portion is inked green  Sectioning reveals firm  white tan  focally  red and gritty  irregular breast parenchyma extending to the inked margins  A representative section of the firm area 1 5cm from lateral edge is frozen as FX 1  Another firm area  1cm in diameterm  0 1cm from the inked margin  lies adjacent to the short suture is frozen as FX 2  The FX 2 is sent to Cox 5  SECTION CODE  A M  entire breast parenchyma  from superior portion to inferior portion  N  FX 1  lateral margin  Labeled  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal firm  white tan  focally yellow  focally cystic  irregular  cut surfaces  submitted entirely in O through S  Labeled  left axillary contents   is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing several lymph nodes  ranging in largest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  The larger ones have whitish tan solid cut surface  Representative half of each lymph node is submitted in T and U  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT LATERAL  BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  BREAST LEFT SUPERIOR   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA    TUBULAR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  2 SPECIMENS  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
