yma blends into the nodular area  1  already described in the medial aspect of the specimen  Within the area of the dense breast parenchyma are grossly visible areas of calcification  A gross photograph of the specimen was taken  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections nodular area  1  to anterior  posterior  and medial margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections nodular area  1  to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections through dense breast parenchyma  area  2   to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section through dense breast parenchyma  area  2  to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of grossly uninvolved breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional lateral margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional anterior medial margin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional superior lateral margin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional posterior margin Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right axillary sentinel node   387   is a piece of fibrofatty tissue  containing a candidate lymph node that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The cut surface of the lymph node appears to have a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm nodule within it that has a firm consistency and a tan white color  The specimen is trisected and submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right axillary sentinel node  247   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibrofatty tissue containing a lymph node  which is trisected and entirely submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of dense breast tissue  The specimen is unoriented and is inked black  The specimen