ellow foci  The remainder of the tissue  approximately 85   consists of adipose tissue with the remaining tissue being soft  white fibrous tissue  The lesion is entirely submitted as A D from the superior to the inferior aspect  Additional sections are submitted as follows  E  Superior end  F  Inferior end  Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue  183   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node  The cut surfaces are soft and tan  The specimen is trisected and entirely submitted as G H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins  medial half of cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm unoriented  irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue  with thermal change  On sectioning no masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue consists mainly of soft  white fibrous tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted as I and J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  lateral half of cavity   are two unoriented irregular portions of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The portions demonstrate thermal artifact  On sectioning no masses or nodules are grossly identified  The tissue is blue dyed stained  The tissue consists of approximately 45  soft  white fibrous tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as K N  Gross Description by  TIM J  ROBINSON Resident  RANIA M  SELIEM  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT SENTINEL  183  EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT SHAVED MARGIN MEDIAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY  E PART D  BREAST RIGHT SHAVED MARGIN LATERAL REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY   , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The invasive tumor has features of both lobular and ductal carcinomas  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm nodular piece of tissue  with a hard tan white cut surface  a portion is frozen as frozen section  1  now submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tissue is submitted entirely in cassettes B and C  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 56 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  30  IN SITU COMPONENT   PRESENT ADJACENT TO THE PREVIOUS BIOPSY SITE WITH A MAXIMUM COMBINED DIMENSION OF REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  NOTE  There is no evidence of malignancy in fourteen of fourteen lymph nodes  No vascular invasion is noted  The resection margins are free of tumor  The carcinoma is similar to the previous pathology   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 14                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a 20 x 16 x 6cm tan yellow modified radical mastectomy specimen including a 18 x 5 5cm tan ellipse of skin with a 2 2cm in diameter unremarkable nippple with a 2 5cm in length  well healed surgical scar directly inferior to the nipple  there is a 12 x 4 x 4cm tan yellow attached axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal multiple semifirm irregular  fibrotic areas deep to the surgical scar measuring 3cm in diameter and present 2cm away from the closest deep margin  Section Code  A  closest deep margin  radial section  B  skin with surgical scar  C E  representative tumor  F  representative fibrotic soft tissue 5cm lateral to the tumor  G H  superior lymph nodes  I  middle lymph nodes  J  inferior lymph nodes  Resident  Horace C  Wu  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Les